 "verdict": {
  "honest_miss": "fid 75 (LOC129526398 = KMT2C exons + TMEM128 exons) is a genuine distributed mosaic but colinear=0.75 (KMT2C covers 6/8 exons) so VG SPARES it at threshold 0.6. Catching it requires threshold>0.75, which would start splitting real alt-first-exon families (fid 288 at 0.75) -> the valley shows 0.6 is the correct precision-preserving choice.",
  "q1_does_colinearity_split_recombinant_over_merges": "YES for 5/10 recombinant blocks (7 bridges): [94, 110, 187, 210, 321]. These are the transitively-merged barbells the pairwise-edge/gamma-quasi-clique graph cannot break (K-frontier / recombination obstruction). VG splits them; density criteria do not. Of the 5 split blocks, 4 are true DISTRIBUTED exon-shuffles [94, 110, 187, 210] (sub-families Mb apart / different chroms) and 1 are READTHROUGH chimeras [321] (genomically-overlapping adjacent genes = assembly artifact, not reshuffling). High-confidence distributed mosaics (both sub-families annotated, minor block >=2 exons): [187, 210].",
  "q2_spares_real_families_recall_cost": "YES. false_split_rate=0.0 (0/24 pure single-gene multi-copy families wrongly split at colinear>=0.6, and 0 across the whole 0.50-0.80 sweep). The pure control carries 0 alt-first-exon families, so the alt-first-exon / alt-TSS recall risk is instead demonstrated DIRECTLY by the SPARED recombinant bridges: fid 288 (DDX11 alt-first-exon, colinear 0.75), fid 339/443 (terminal-exon variants, colinear 0.75-0.94) are all correctly SPARED at threshold 0.6. Each would only be wrongly split above its own colinear cover (>=0.75), which is why the sweep's block count jumps 5->10 only at threshold 0.80.",
  "q3_net_worthwhile": "WORTHWHILE ON ITS NICHE, NOT A HEADLINE LEVER. Reshuffling is REAL but the smallest bucket: 10/83 over-merged blocks are recombinant, of which VG cleanly splits 5 at ZERO recall cost. The flagship is fid 210 (LOC115935264 = LOC101126070 exons + GALNT17 exons), the exact G1-G2-G3 barbell. Residual over-merge is dominated by sub-exonic repeat bridges (34) + cardinality (19) + domain-share (20), which recombination-detection does NOT address. Net precision gain ~5/606 blocks (~0.8 pt)."
 },
